    "headline": "Air India's consolidated loss widens to Rs 22,238 crore in FY26",
    "body": "Air India's consolidated loss widened to over Rs 22,000 crore in fiscal 2025-26. Total income declined while total expenses increased during the same financial period. Aircraft repair costs rose, but fuel expenses saw a decrease. Foreign exchange losses significantly increased, impacting the airline's financial performance. The company expects insurance to cover liabilities from the AI171 accident.",
